 ### 2+D Pen-and-Ink for Volume Visualization
-- **Definition**: A method where 2D strokes are generated based on 3D information associated with original 3D objects, treating isosurfaces as opaque objects for image buffer generation [S1, unofficial].
-- **Steps**: Extract isosurfaces from the raw dataset [S1, unofficial]. Treat isosurfaces as opaque objects for the generation of image buffers [S1, unofficial]. Generate image buffers representing properties including lighting, depth, normals, horizontal curvature, and vertical curvature [S1, unofficial]. Use these image buffers as inputs to different pen-and-ink filters to synthesize a final image [S1, unofficial].
+A method where 2D strokes are generated based on 3D information associated with original 3D objects, treating isosurfaces as opaque objects for image buffer generation [S1, unofficial]. It extracts isosurfaces from the raw dataset, treats them as opaque objects for generating image buffers representing properties including lighting, depth, normals, horizontal curvature, and vertical curvature, and uses these buffers as inputs to different pen-and-ink filters to synthesize a final image [S1, unofficial]. Choose it for generating non-photorealistic, hand-drawn style illustrations from volume datasets with minimal user interaction [S1, unofficial].
 
